{"kind":"finding","id":"F-trajectory-orbit-018-01","file":"Source/Parsek.Tests/ReaimedTrajectoryTests.cs","line":89,"method":"Adapter_NullOrEmptyAssembled_FallsBackToInnerSpan","category":"T1","severity":"Medium","confidence":"high","falsifiability":"falsifiability: Source/Parsek/Reaim/ReaimedTrajectory.cs:81-82; stubbing the else branch to spanStartUT = spanEndUT = 0.0 leaves this GREEN; dropping the null-coalesce at line 72 -> red","what_it_asserts":"HasOrbitSegments is false and OrbitSegments is empty when the assembled list is null.","why_weak":"The named behavior (span falls back to the inner trajectory) lives at lines 79-83 and is never read: StartUT and EndUT are not asserted, so the fallback could return 0/0 and the test still passes.","proposed_action":"Assert adapter.StartUT and adapter.EndUT equal the wrapped recording's span, and add the empty-list case alongside the null case so both halves of OrNull/OrEmpty are covered.","effort":"S","july_ref":"none"}
